{"name":"Squid Hat","hex":"#6e2233","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"squid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several carnivorous marine cephalopod mollusks, of the order Teuthida, having a mantle, eight arms, and a pair of tentacles.","A fishhook with a piece of bright lead, bone, or other substance fastened on its shank to imitate a squid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish with a squid fishhook.","To cause squidding (an improper, partial, parachute inflation, that results in the sides of the parachute folding in on the center, and pulsating back and forth)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squid"},{"term":"hat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Haitian Creole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covering for the head, often in the approximate form of a cone, dome or  cylinder closed at its top end, and sometimes having a brim and other decoration.","A particular role or capacity that a person might fill."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Squid","blocks":[{"text":"A squid is a mollusc with an elongated soft body, large eyes, eight arms, and two tentacles in the orders Myopsida, Oegopsida, and Bathyteuthida. Like all other cephalopods, squid have a distinct head, bilateral symmetry, and a mantle. They are mainly soft-bodied, like octopuses, but have a small internal skeleton in the form of a rod-like gladius or pen, made of chitin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg/330px-Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squid","wikidata":"Q81900"},{"title":"Hat","blocks":[{"text":"A hat is a head covering which is worn for various reasons, including protection against weather conditions, ceremonial reasons such as university graduation, religious reasons, comedy, safety, or as a fashion accessory. Hats which incorporate mechanical features, such as visors, spikes, flaps, braces or beer holders shade into the broader category of headgear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Chapeaux_en_peau_de_castor.jpg/330px-Chapeaux_en_peau_de_castor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hat","wikidata":"Q80151"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg/500px-Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg/1280px-Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg/500px-Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASepioteuthis_sepioidea_(Caribbean_Reef_Squid).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Nautilus_belauensis_profile_%28white_background%29.jpg/500px-Nautilus_belauensis_profile_%28white_background%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Nautilus_belauensis_profile_%28white_background%29.jpg/500px-Nautilus_belauensis_profile_%28white_background%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANautilus_belauensis_profile_(white_background).jpg"},{"srcset":